# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Large input data -- regenerable, and far past what GitHub will take.
# high_cov/vcf alone is 32 GB across 44 phased VCFs averaging ~730 MB each;
# GitHub's hard limit is 100 MB per file, so these can never be committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
new_pipeline/real_data/high_cov/vcf/
new_pipeline/real_data/merged_pruned/
new_pipeline/real_data/hapibd_work/
new_pipeline/plink_output/
new_pipeline/fastsmc_work/
*.vcf
*.vcf.gz
*.bcf
*.bed
*.bim
*.fam
!new_pipeline/real_data/high_cov/bad_regions_grch38.bed
!new_pipeline/real_data/high_cov/reference_masks/*.bed

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Third-party tools installed into the tree, not our code.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
new_pipeline/real_data/tools/HapNe/
*.jar

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build artifacts.  cmdstanpy compiles each .stan into a same-named Mach-O
# executable next to it; those were tracked, so every recompile wrote another
# ~4 MB blob into history (18 of them, 60 MB per full rebuild).  The .stan
# source is the artifact worth keeping -- the binary is machine-specific and
# rebuilt automatically on first use.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
new_pipeline/models/ibd_model_N*
new_pipeline/models/mixed_model_N*
new_pipeline/models/snp_model_N*
new_pipeline/real_data/ibd_model_N*
new_pipeline/real_data/mixed_model_N*
new_pipeline/real_data/snp_model_N*
!*.stan
*.hpp
*.o
*.d

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
